R3472 frontdoor head-grammar evidence
===== leg 1: read-only probe before the edit (31 shapes, tmp/probe-R3472.py + tmp/probe-R3472b.py)
two-word request lines were answered in HTTP/0.9 mode with no header block at all:
  GET /healthz                -> raw "ok"
  GET /                       -> raw root HTML
  GET HTTP/1.1 + Host         -> raw "404 not found"
  GET  HTTP/1.1 + Host        -> raw "404 not found"
a non-origin target was read as the root:
  GET ?x=1 HTTP/1.1           -> 200 root page
header grammar had no enforcement:
  Bad Header: x               -> 200 ok
  Bad\x01Header: x            -> 200 ok
  : x                         -> 200 ok
  JUNKLINE (no colon)         -> 200 ok
  X-A: a then " b" (obs-fold) -> 200 ok
  X-A: a\x00b                 -> 200 ok
framing values:
  Content-Length: 5 + 6       -> 200 ok
  Content-Length: 5, 6        -> 200 ok
block limits were already policed by the stdlib through this door:
  70000-byte header line      -> 431 Line too long, policy, close
  101 fields                  -> 431 Too many headers, policy, close
===== leg 2: the same probe after the edit
  four malformed request lines -> 400 "400 bad request line" with status line,
                                  policy, Content-Length and Connection: close
  ?x=1                         -> 400 "400 bad request target"
  three bad field names        -> 400 "400 invalid header name"
  obs-fold (two shapes)        -> 400 "400 folded header line"
  colonless line               -> 400 "400 malformed header line"
  NUL in a value               -> 400 "400 invalid header value"
  CL 5/6 and CL "5, 6"         -> 400 "400 conflicting content length"
  CL 5/5 (equal duplicates)    -> 200 ok with Connection: close
  HTAB in a value              -> 200 ok
  GET * HTTP/1.1               -> 404 not found with a status line (grammar only)
  431 shapes                   -> unchanged, policy, close
